# Generated intermediates. tools/gif-to-grid.mjs rebuilds these from the delivered animations in
# art-source/gif/ (lossless animated WebP now), which ARE committed — so they are ~10MB of PNG that a checkout
# does not need. Regenerate with:
#   node tools/gif-to-grid.mjs sprite-max-px-frames-36-rows-6-cols-6.webp  run-gif.png
#   node tools/gif-to-grid.mjs sprite-max-px-frames-36-rows-6-cols-6-2.webp jump-gif.png
#   node tools/gif-to-grid.mjs skid-new.webp skid-new-gif.png
#   node tools/gif-to-grid.mjs ko-new.webp   ko-new-gif.png
#   node tools/slice-char.mjs
# and the tremble grid from the owner's delivered sheet (tremble-src.webp IS committed):
#   node tools/sheet-to-grid.mjs tremble-src.webp tremble-new.png --rows=3 --cols=4
art-source/char-sheets/*-gif.png
art-source/char-sheets/tremble-new.png

# Evidence frames for a QA report — regenerate with: node tools/qa-evidence.mjs
qa-report/
art-source/char-sheets/idle-sheet.png
*.tmp.mjs


# Scratch from making Part 2's voice and jump: pitch and style probes, a draft take and a
# review screenshot. The real sources are art-source/audio-source/part2-vo/ (read by
# tools/assemble-part2-vo.mjs) and the GIF that tools/build-jump-cycle.mjs slices.
art-source/audio-source/*-probe.pcm
art-source/audio-source/*-probe.wav
art-source/audio-source/*-draft.wav
art-source/audio-source/vo-style-sample.mp3
art-source/jump-landing-review.png
